{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787081954504827002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"blusterous-earthly-kitten","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"5357c95f149e79449c26b544b0b04268d780ccc49f662fb05a101169c35e4b58","event_uuid":"dad26d60-e06d-431a-ae9d-cb2e7db072da","position":{"commit_sha":"7ad9d24e9368066fccf8faf83f781e155440fdf7","position":"1787080915641487001-dad26d60-e06d-431a-ae9d-cb2e7db072da"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"81295c8424b52e8a0313a61b06cc96f0f91afd64f49d0318923b471cad90860f","event_uuid":"a635dd7f-3f4b-459b-89d1-153cd197b73d","position":{"commit_sha":"1b36f98abe3dce3a7501c4260891a8306fca0118","position":"1787080920799964001-a635dd7f-3f4b-459b-89d1-153cd197b73d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8d9ea5a2000e6404ecf3e11d287795f40b11d75fbc7c3b79c123f09411d4f27c","event_uuid":"3557345a-8763-43eb-bd88-7bc036c6e061","position":{"commit_sha":"7ca9d3a4ef1941672fffb64c7f3027705f93b223","position":"1787081946633785001-3557345a-8763-43eb-bd88-7bc036c6e061"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2b9953c52b0168976e4fa81f289a92ba15bf8c3508b5f5e63fe0f6725728eeda","event_uuid":"fb28fa4d-a8fe-42d2-883e-20a8648ad779","position":{"commit_sha":"881dd27b3bb1a10773db60c4c614235709a77d4b","position":"1787081954504827001-fb28fa4d-a8fe-42d2-883e-20a8648ad779"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787080915641487001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a635dd7f-3f4b-459b-89d1-153cd197b73d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ba48-a88a-92bd-45d0"}],"description":"Remove the deprecated force_close INPUT surface so the write-op parity oracle needs zero exceptions. Operator ruling (2026-08-18): remove deprecated flags/verbs rather than exempt or mirror them. force is the sanctioned gate-bypass across all surfaces; force_close is its deprecated predecessor.\n\n## Context / Problem\nKeeping force_close as an accepted INPUT would force the parity oracle to carry an exception (or mirror a dead flag onto MCP just to match). Removing the input surface lets the oracle assert total parity with no allow-list. The surviving force=True path already covers the operator use case force_close served (a closed-without-signed-attestation audit signal).\n\n## Approach\nRetire force_close as an accepted INPUT on the lib and CLI ONLY, routed through the supported rebar._deprecations warn/tombstone path. CRITICAL event-sourcing caveat: force_close is not only an input — it also lives in the event schema + reducer (schemas/ticket_state.schema.json, reducer/_processors_status.py, _commands/txn.py, transition_close.py, close_precheck.py, types.py). This is an event-sourced store, so historical events carrying force_close MUST keep reducing to the same state. This is therefore a tombstone of the INPUT surface, NOT a hard delete: the reducer and schema keep tolerating historical force_close events unchanged.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_lib_writes.py — remove force_close as an accepted transition() input param; warn-tombstone it via rebar._deprecations.\n- src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py (and the close disposition/precheck input path) — remove the CLI force_close input spelling; warn-tombstone.\n- src/rebar/_deprecations.py — register the force_close input tombstone.\n- Reducer/schema (reducer/_processors_status.py, schemas/ticket_state.schema.json, _commands/txn.py, types.py) — INTENTIONALLY UNCHANGED for historical-event tolerance.\n- Sweep the lib/CLI/MCP write verbs for any other deprecated input flag that would otherwise require an oracle exception; record findings on the ticket.\n\n## Testing\n- Passing force_close as an input emits a rebar._deprecations warning and is no longer an accepted param (unit test asserts the warning and that it is not honored as a live bypass).\n- A fixture event stream carrying a historical force_close event still reduces to the identical ticket state (reducer back-compat test).\n- The parity oracle (sibling topaz-blubbery-mice) carries no force_close row/exception and still passes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Passing force_close as an input WARNs via rebar._deprecations and is no longer a supported live param (unit test).\n- [ ] Docs and docstrings no longer advertise force_close as a usable input (grep is clean).\n- [ ] A historical event carrying force_close still reduces to the same ticket state (reducer fixture test passes).\n- [ ] The parity oracle carries no force_close exception and passes.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` are green.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_writes.py","reason":"remove force_close input param; warn-tombstone via _deprecations"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","reason":"remove CLI force_close input spelling; warn-tombstone"},{"path":"src/rebar/_deprecations.py","reason":"register the force_close input tombstone"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_force_close_tombstone.py","reason":"new: deprecation-warn test + reducer historical-event back-compat test"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"73b2-6194-c430-45ab","ticket_type":"task","title":"Remove deprecated force_close input surface (tombstone; keep reducer back-compat)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["dad26d60-e06d-431a-ae9d-cb2e7db072da","a635dd7f-3f4b-459b-89d1-153cd197b73d","3557345a-8763-43eb-bd88-7bc036c6e061","fb28fa4d-a8fe-42d2-883e-20a8648ad779"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787081954504827002,"uuid":"c8a44ca6-9776-491a-ba72-986f567ca41f"}